  "id": "mate-guarding",
  "term": "mate guarding",
  "definition": "Mate guarding is a reproductive behavior in which one animal keeps hold of a potential mating partner before copulation. In the source described here, a male copepod clasps another individual, usually a female, and maintains the pair until mating unless the captured individual actively rejects the attempt.",
